## Generated Object, Generated Phenomenon

This is the first place where "hole" is a settled object-name, but the
object-name is not free. The generated ascent is:

* process: causal reachability to a chosen readout;
* structure: the partition into no-readout interior, readout exterior, and
  shroud;
* force-site: an effect relation whose sources are restricted to the shroud;
* object: the bundled `Hole`;
* phenomenon: effects can occur only from the generated boundary side.

The last line is checked rather than asserted by analogy:

{docstring Obsmetrologia.CausalSets.BlackHoles.Hole.effect_source_interior}

{docstring Obsmetrologia.CausalSets.BlackHoles.Hole.effect_source_not_exterior}

and for the canonical no-readout object:

{docstring Obsmetrologia.CausalSets.BlackHoles.Hole.ofReadout_effect_source_interior}

{docstring Obsmetrologia.CausalSets.BlackHoles.Hole.ofReadout_effect_source_not_exterior}

Checked:

```lean
example {E : Type} (H : Hole E) {x y : E}
    (h : H.effect x y) :
    H.interior x = true :=
  H.effect_source_interior h

example {E : Type} (H : Hole E) {x y : E}
    (h : H.effect x y) :
    H.exterior x = false :=
  H.effect_source_not_exterior h

example {E : Type} (C : CausalSet E)
    [CausalLeDecision C] (readout : FiniteHoleRegion E)
    {x y : E}
    (h : (Hole.ofReadout C readout).effect x y) :
    (Hole.ofReadout C readout).interior x = true :=
  Hole.ofReadout_effect_source_interior C readout h
```

This is the lawful "hole" reading in mereological language: the interior is not
an extra object placed inside an ambient container. It is the complement of
readout reachability, with a shroud where the surrounding causal structure can
encounter it. The effect law turns that boundary into a force-site, but it does
not yet prove entropy, area, Hawking radiation, information recovery, or smooth
horizon geometry.

## Phase Boundary

This is also the lawful boundary for any later "hole matter" phrase. The
settled object is a finite no-readout carrier with a shroud and shroud-sourced
effects. Calling it a black-hole reading is a physical reading of that carrier,
not an additional theorem. Calling a horizon-bearing system an agent is likewise
frontier unless a later page constructs the transport from no-readout boundary
behavior to agency-bearing organization.

The page may therefore promote only this much: a causal region can fail to reach
readout; that no-readout region is future closed; its exterior is past closed;
the shroud is an interior boundary adjacent to the exterior; and bundled effects
must originate on that shroud side. The manual must not infer agency, entropy,
area, radiation, or recovery from the word "hole."

## Repair Path

If this page overreaches, demote the claim to frontier unless the missing carrier
is built. A promotion path would add, in order: a lawful conformal-infinity
carrier, a boundary topology or smooth null-hypersurface carrier, an area
functional, and then thermodynamic or quantum-information structure. Until then,
the settled object is the no-readout closure site above.
